  "authoringNote": "The case assessmentDate and the explicit argument are both the valid ISO date 2026-10-19, so there is no assessment_date_invalid or assessment_date_mismatch rejection. The reviewed pack lists only 2026-10-18 in supportedAssessmentDates, so R08 holds R08.assessment_date_unsupported: conflict for the administrative reviewer with the scope_hold effect, naming no document, and the state is scope_hold. The pack ID matches and the pack is reviewed and sourced. No date is added to the pack. The case and record supplier interval 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31 contains 2026-10-19, so no R01 interval condition holds and R01 passes citing the eight supplier and order item code facts. Every other finding follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and final signed order (2026-09-04) name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001, and the order is after the encounter and within the C01 bound 2027-02-26; the receipt references the order version and is recorded at 2026-09-05T18:40:00Z, after the C06 span 2026-09-03T10:00:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z of the date-only order; the named supplier record is usable and hash-valid. R02 passes with six beneficiary citations (encounter, order, receipt), R03 passes with nine, R04 with six (status, date and practitioner identifier of each final document; null times supply no fact), R05 with four. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false; no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R09 passes. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. Quarantine and superseded lists are empty and clinicalReviewRequired is true. Parent affectedDocuments are empty: no held condition is restricted, unreadable or failed provenance (C07).",
